WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.578
Sleeping well on board: why it's hard, and
what really helps.

2
00:00:05.828 --> 00:00:09.197
The station circles the Earth about every
ninety minutes.

3
00:00:09.237 --> 00:00:11.296
That's sixteen sunrises a day.

4
00:00:12.196 --> 00:00:16.642
Add the hum of the fans and the excitement
of the mission, and nights get short.

5
00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:19.691
Lucas lies awake, his mind still racing.

6
00:00:20.591 --> 00:00:24.588
Studies found astronauts sleep about six
hours a night on average,

7
00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:27.314
less than the seven or more that adults
need.

8
00:00:28.214 --> 00:00:31.323
Protect your sleep. Dim the lights an hour
before

9
00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:33.798
bed, and use the eye mask and earplugs.

10
00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:38.833
Keep the same bedtime every day, and skip
coffee in the afternoon.

11
00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:43.131
Log your nights in AURA, in ten seconds
each morning,

12
00:00:43.131 --> 00:00:45.375
so a bad streak gets noticed early.

13
00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:50.006
And never take a sleeping pill without
asking Keiko first.

14
00:00:50.906 --> 00:00:54.918
A rested crew is a safer crew: fewer
mistakes, and a better mood.

